    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "paragraph_number": 189,
      "text": "Values are median [Q1, Q3] or n/N (%), unless stated otherwise. The external analysis unit is the hospitalization episode; patient identity is the clustering unit for uncertainty estimation. Patient-contribution percentages use 50 patients; race/ethnicity percentages use 102 episodes. ICU length of stay is summarized among the 13 ICU-exposed episodes.",
      "display_html": "Values are median [Q1, Q3] or n/N (%), unless stated otherwise. The external analysis unit is the hospitalization episode; patient identity is the clustering unit for uncertainty estimation. Patient-contribution percentages use 50 patients; race/ethnicity percentages use 102 episodes. ICU length of stay is summarized among the 13 ICU-exposed episodes."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "paragraph_number": 190,
      "text": "Index decompensation manifestations are based on the previously adjudicated MIMIC-specific structured-data assessment. They are not mutually exclusive; denominators reflect available adjudicated phenotype-support information. Race/ethnicity categories were collapsed from recorded MIMIC-IV categories for description.",
      "display_html": "Index decompensation manifestations are based on the previously adjudicated MIMIC-specific structured-data assessment. They are not mutually exclusive; denominators reflect available adjudicated phenotype-support information. Race/ethnicity categories were collapsed from recorded MIMIC-IV categories for description."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "paragraph_number": 191,
      "text": "SMD is domestic minus external using pooled standard deviations; positive values indicate higher domestic values. SMDs describe case mix and were not used for hypothesis testing or model selection. Domestic predictors reflected index-admission status; external values were aligned to admission as closely as available data allowed. These comparisons do not establish causal explanations for performance differences.",
      "display_html": "SMD is domestic minus external using pooled standard deviations; positive values indicate higher domestic values. SMDs describe case mix and were not used for hypothesis testing or model selection. Domestic predictors reflected index-admission status; external values were aligned to admission as closely as available data allowed. These comparisons do not establish causal explanations for performance differences."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "paragraph_number": 192,
      "text": "The admission-oriented observed-measurement hierarchy and its exceptions are described in Note M1.",
      "display_html": "The admission-oriented observed-measurement hierarchy and its exceptions are described in Note M1."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "paragraph_number": 193,
      "text": "Abbreviations: ICU, intensive care unit; MIMIC, Medical Information Mart for Intensive Care; SMD, standardized mean difference; INR, international normalized ratio; ALBI, albumin-bilirubin score; FIB-4, fibrosis-4 index; MELD-Na, Model for End-Stage Liver Disease-sodium; Q1/Q3, first/third quartiles. Core4 comprises INR, platelet count, ALBI and FIB-4.",
      "display_html": "Abbreviations: ICU, intensive care unit; MIMIC, Medical Information Mart for Intensive Care; SMD, standardized mean difference; INR, international normalized ratio; ALBI, albumin-bilirubin score; FIB-4, fibrosis-4 index; MELD-Na, Model for End-Stage Liver Disease-sodium; Q1/Q3, first/third quartiles. Core4 comprises INR, platelet count, ALBI and FIB-4."
    },
